# `results/` — Generated review and reporting outputs

## Authority

The root [`README.md`](../README.md) contract defines what belongs here. Root
and local [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) files prohibit hand-editing generated output.

## Use this directory for

| Path | Contents |
| --- | --- |
| `qc/` | Machine-readable QC, exclusions, and diagnostic records (no plots) |
| `figures/light/` | Canonical print/paper data figures, including QC graphics |
| `figures/dark/` | Screen/dark-theme variants generated from the same sources |
| `tables/` | Terminal report-ready summaries and model outputs |
| `logs/` | Terminal execution logs and diagnostics for the current generated run |
| `resolved_config.yaml` | Resolved configuration for the current execution |
| `provenance.json` | Complete provenance for the current execution |

Everything here is declared pipeline output, ignored by Git, and regenerated.
To change it, edit the producing code or configuration and rerun. Reusable
analysis-ready datasets belong in `data/processed/`, not `results/tables/`.
Non-regenerable authored schematics belong in `assets/figures/`.

Snakemake's own cache/work state remains in `.snakemake/`; place only declared,
human-inspectable terminal logs in `results/logs/`.

Running the pipeline may replace current provenance. Durable registration copies
it to `metadata/provenance/` and appends `metadata/runs.csv`; those actions are
separate and human-approved.
